From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:44:38 +0100
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp: complete the Iris IOMMU and coherency

The Iris node merged in 7.3 lists only stream 0x2a00 and is not marked
dma-coherent. The Dragon Q8B series carried the full node from Radxa
with a second stream, 0x2a07, and dma-coherent, and Iris decode and
encode were validated with it, so keep those two properties.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
@@ -4264,8 +4264,10 @@ &config_noc SLAVE_VENUS_CFG QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>,
 					     "video-mem";
 
 			operating-points-v2 = <&iris_opp_table>;
-			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x2a00 0x400>;
+			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x2a00 0x400>,
+				 <&apps_smmu 0x2a07 0x400>;
 			memory-region = <&pil_video_mem>;
+			dma-coherent;
 
 			status = "disabled";
 
-- 
Armbian

